From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: a native DLL mapped only to be read is that file
 (5957)

NtMapViewOfSection put Wine's builtin in place of any image mapped whose
name it has, also when the view was only to be read:
LOAD_LIBRARY_AS_IMAGE_RESOURCE (GetFileVersionInfo, icons, strings). An
application's own vcruntime140.dll / msvcp140.dll / ucrtbase.dll then read
as the builtin's, newer, version, and Windows Installer kept it at every
uninstall ("newer version detected"): Temurin, Corretto and Foxit left
their runtime DLLs in Program Files (qa5 2026-10-22). On Windows such a
view is the file. A view to run code (the loader's, executable) still
takes the builtin.
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
index 5136290..7550cbb 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -3242,7 +3242,17 @@ static unsigned int virtual_map_section( HANDLE handle, PVOID *addr_ptr, ULONG_P
             NtCurrentTeb64()->Tib.ArbitraryUserPointer = PtrToUlong(NtCurrentTeb()->Tib.ArbitraryUserPointer);
         }
         filename = (WCHAR *)(image_info + 1);
-        /* check if we can replace that mapping with the builtin */
+        /* check if we can replace that mapping with the builtin -- when it is to run. A view that
+           only reads a native file (LOAD_LIBRARY_AS_IMAGE_RESOURCE: its version, its icons) is that
+           file's, as on Windows: an application's own vcruntime140.dll read as the builtin's,
+           newer, version, and Windows Installer kept it at every uninstall (Temurin, Corretto,
+           Foxit; qa5 2026-10-22) */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_READVIEW_BUILTIN
+        if (!(protect & (PAGE_EXECUTE | PAGE_EXECUTE_READ | PAGE_EXECUTE_READWRITE | PAGE_EXECUTE_WRITECOPY)) &&
+            !image_info->wine_builtin && !image_info->wine_fakedll)
+            res = STATUS_IMAGE_ALREADY_LOADED;
+        else
+#endif
         res = load_builtin( image_info, filename, machine, &info,
                             addr_ptr, size_ptr, limit_low, limit_high );
         if (res == STATUS_IMAGE_ALREADY_LOADED)
